Practical 3 :-
Write a Prolog program to perform list manipulation operations (appending two lists, reversing a list, and searching for an element).

Prolog code:-
% Append two lists
my_append([], L, L).

my_append([H|T], L, [H|R]) :-
    my_append(T, L, R).

% Reverse a list
my_reverse([], []).

my_reverse([H|T], R) :-
    my_reverse(T, RT),
    my_append(RT, [H], R).

% Search for an element
my_member(X, [X|_]).

my_member(X, [_|T]) :-
    my_member(X, T).

% Find the length of a list
my_length([], 0).

my_length([_|T], N) :-
    my_length(T, N1),
    N is N1 + 1.


